  "matching_notes": [
    "source_prefix is retained for integration compatibility, but source_package must match EXACTLY after parsing source RPM filename or dpkg source:Package. Do not use an unrestricted startswith test.",
    "These are two-CVE fixed minima, not newest available versions; require exact OS release, branch, source name, official signed origin and native EVR comparison. Never use sort -V or PHP_VERSION alone for vendor backports.",
    "For RPM, split version-release into native fields and preserve package epoch from trusted repository metadata; ALAS pages cited here publish version-release and do not establish a machine-read epoch.",
    "Proof of an installed fixed package does not prove running workers were replaced; runtime executable/module-to-package mapping and full worker restart are separate required checks.",
    "Missing policy, pending/no-fix status, missing signed candidate, metadata failure, incompatible transaction, and provenance ambiguity are unresolved and must not exit success.",
    "ondrej-apt rules require one authenticated origin record matching every apt_origin field, the exact OS release, PHP 7.4 source and native package/source version matching version_regex. installed_version_regex only constrains vendor lineage; it is not proof of a fixed installation. Current repository metadata must authenticate both planning and execution."
  ],
